// trap: a safety cone whose only counterexample runs a handler before its raiser (#206).
// Ship runs on EvApproved, which Approve raises, and Approve needs the order paid. The rule
// reads the status and the payment, not the approval, so its cone leaves the mark and
// Approve out and runs Ship unordered: place, ship, and the order is shipped unpaid. In the
// whole model Ship runs only after Approve, so only on a paid order, and no delete resets the
// payment: the rule holds. The counterexample does not replay on the cone widened with the
// mark and its raiser, and the widened cone holds, so the native checker says ok. TLC checks
// the cone as it is and finds the unordered run (docs/engine-agreement.md, rule 1). z3 reads
// the order and proves the rule.
// expect Forbidden_Order_0: native=ok tlc=counterexample z3=proved bfs=ok,ok,ok
entity Order "注文" {
  id: Int @pk
  status: Enum(pending, shipped) @default(pending)
  paid: Bool @default(false)
  approved: Bool @default(false)
}
usecase Place "注文"
usecase Pay "支払い"
usecase Approve "承認"
usecase Ship "出荷"
event EvApproved "承認済"
creates(Place, Order)
sets(Pay, Order.paid == true)
sets(Approve, Order.approved == true)
raises(Approve, EvApproved)
triggers(EvApproved, Ship)
transitions(Ship, Order.status, pending -> shipped)
condition Paid "支払済"
holds(Paid, Order.paid == true)
applies_to(Paid, Approve)
forbidden(Order, status == shipped, paid == false)
